From df1916927f7737427bb67f68d5cd2d7fe681b5db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:01:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: enable the display backlight

The backlight node was fully described but disabled because there was
no panel driver to light it up for. It drives DISP_PWM channel 0 of
mmsys (stock disp_pwm0@1100e000, SPI 128 - identical to the mt8183.dtsi
pwm0 node) and enables the LED string through GPIO56
(odm/lcd-backlight, led_mode = 5 = PWM).

pwm0 is provided by pwm-mtk-disp (mediatek,mt8183-disp-pwm), which is
already built in (CONFIG_PWM_MTK_DISP), and its power domain is the
DISP one that the panel path needs anyway.

If the panel is enabled but the screen stays black, dropping
"status = okay" here is the fastest way to tell "no picture" from "no
backlight".
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index bfd2b21ad..e948e27ed 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ backlight: backlight {
 		brightness-levels = <0 1023>;
 		num-interpolated-steps = <1023>;
 		default-brightness-level = <576>;
-		status = "disabled";
+		status = "okay";
 	};
 
 	/* Dual-cell LiHV pack (stock: 8 Ah, 4.35 V/cell). */
-- 
